{"text": "7 Heast of Global Complionrce\n\nFrom: Lea, Melissa\nSent: 11 September 2016 09:03 PM\nTo: Higginson, Anette <anette.higginson@sap.com>\n\nCe:\n. Subject: Re: [CONFIDENTIAL] URGENT: Request for Global Compliance review of SAP Partners in South Africa\n\nSensitivity: Confidential\n\nExcellent work here, seems all steps have been taken to do the best validation possible. | approve continuing the\n\npartnerships.\nMelissa\n\n\u201cSent from my iPhone *\n\nOw'Sep 10, 2016, at 5:51 AM, Higginson, Anette <1.0 66 cog niu sap.com> wrote:\nDear Melissa,\n\nRe: CAD House (current 3rdP Sales Commission Partner), Global Softech Solutions (GSS) (current\nReseller and SI Partner), Cutting Edge (prospective new Reseller Partner) .\n\nIn South Africa, a local family \u201cthe Guptas\u201d has received a wide range of press, business and\ngovernment interest due to their connections to our State President and influence in\ngovernment. Due to pressure from banks, audit firms, stock exchange and private business, the\nGuptas have been forced to divest from South Africa and have moved to the Emirates.\n\nWe found evidence that Sahara Systenss (Gupta owned) acquired majority shareholding of the\naforementioned SAP Partners in approximately April 2016. Subsequently, Sahara Systems have sold\ntheir shareholding to Futureteg (no Gupta ownership). We have attached forensic reports\nconfirming that the sale of business is currently in process with our focal authorities (CIPC). The new\n1",
